From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: compute shaders and unordered access views (feature level 11_0, stage 2)

- Compute shaders: thread group size, the thread IDs (vThreadID as group * size + in group), group shared memory
  (every g# region in TGSI's one shared block, its size the compute state's), sync as MEMBAR + BARRIER.
  CreateComputeShader, CsSet*, Dispatch and DispatchIndirect; a memory barrier after each dispatch and after draws
  whose pixel shader writes UAVs (D3D orders UAV writes before later work, GL needs barriers).
- UAVs: typed ones are TGSI images, raw and structured ones TGSI buffers (byte addresses; structured: index *
  stride + offset), as are raw and structured shader resource views; loads, stores, atomics with and without the
  old value, append/consume through a hidden counter buffer per UAV (initial counts, CopyStructureCount),
  bufinfo/resinfo, UAV clears (uint bits per channel, float converted; buffers filled: virgl has no buffer
  clears). Pixel shader UAVs from SetRenderTargets.
- What a shader uses is bound at draw/dispatch time (Shader_bindings: textures, images, buffers).
- Typed UAV images get the bound view's format: virglrenderer declares format-less (store-only) images rgba32f,
  a format mismatch with any other format, so shaders are translated again for the bound formats (a few variants
  kept per shader). UAVs are coherent where the shader has UAV barriers (GLSL makes other invocations' writes
  visible to coherent accesses only).
- Resources: the structured stride from the 11 creation arguments; UAV textures carry a sampler view bind
  (virgl passes no image bind and virglrenderer refuses textures without one), buffers a shader buffer bind.
- Fixes found on the way, also for D3D10:
  - integer negate modifiers (iadd r0, -r1, l(3)) became float negations in virglrenderer: INEG now.
  - read maps of 3D textures read each slice separately: virglrenderer reads back only a box's first slice.
- The parser takes zero-component operands of shader model 5 (UAVs, group shared memory, streams).
---
